{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550664-have-you-ever-considered-the-difference-between-ancient-and-modern-foods-in-roleplay","id":1550664,"title":"Have you ever considered the difference between ancient and modern foods in roleplay?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-04T08:43:27-07:00","id":1550664,"title":"Have you ever considered the difference between ancient and modern foods in roleplay?","content":"Like for example imagine a Kindred with the Eat Food Merit, realizing certain things, like that certain fruits and vegetables are no longer being grown or that Carrots are orange now instead of purple. There was also a particular spice used during the days of Ancient Rome that no longer exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-HfljPdCEC8?si=lJBdX7E0bN4o3VLM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-HfljPdCEC8?si=lJBdX7E0bN4o3VLM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-HfljPdCEC8?si=lJBdX7E0bN4o3VLM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/-HfljPdCEC8?si=lJBdX7E0bN4o3VLM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/XPFIwlUeNQU?si=soZb5X-w7s09yfh4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/XPFIwlUeNQU?si=soZb5X-w7s09yfh4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/XPFIwlUeNQU?si=soZb5X-w7s09yfh4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/XPFIwlUeNQU?si=soZb5X-w7s09yfh4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/SJnIZiH5fyM?si=qA5BPt3UPiEJksae\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/SJnIZiH5fyM?si=qA5BPt3UPiEJksae\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/SJnIZiH5fyM?si=qA5BPt3UPiEJksae\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/SJnIZiH5fyM?si=qA5BPt3UPiEJksae </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 05-04-2025, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T02:24:07-07:00","id":1550679,"title":"","content":"Kinda?<br /> <br /> The problem is the circumstances where it matters are kinda limited in either applicability or in fun.<br /> <br /> If you're running a game set in Rome or Byzantium in the classical era, food and how people interacted with it in their daily lives would have been very different... but also not. There are just certain practicalities to urban life even in ancient times that cause food history to rhyme if not repeat. Once you have cities, you have lower class people that need to eat but aren't agricultural workers that feed themselves along with paying their rent to their local ruler(s). Cities are trade hubs that bring in cuisines, staple foods, and spices from a much wider number of areas than was previously available. However, that's also a level of immersion a lot of people don't want to have to remember in play, just like they don't want to have to study the languages of the time period either. <br /> <br /> In many regards eating customs are more important than specific food items because food is a big part of human social interactions (and there is a noticeable psychological impact of human customs with how taste is perceived).<br /> <br /> But yeah, sure, for the tiny handful of characters in the WoD that are both long lived enough to have experienced multiple waves of different cuisines dominate a given area, and actually been focused enough on food despite probably not needing it if they're immortal on that level, it could be an interesting quirk/hobby for the character to indulge in and give them a bit more flavor (pun intended) in what sort of things occupy their time when they're not doing important plot stuff. In a modern day chronicle, this is rarely going to be the PCs, so it's probably an NPC... which means again, the players need to enjoy this particular character's love of food history and epicurean adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T12:35:27-07:00","id":1550701,"title":"","content":"For Vampires and the rare old Ghoul, the problem is that their blood thirst kind of overshadows most other passions they might have, but I think especially food if they still can consume it. I could see some Elder still having a bunch of Silphium in their garden for when they want to indulge in some nostalgia though.<br /> <br /> The one splat I think this would affect the most are probably Mummies, and having one with a passion for food and cooking could be a fitting character quirk for them. I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> on this though, the concept probably works best as an NPC encounter. If you want to go Hannibal Lector, there's also a cult of mortals who gain power from eating supernaturals (the Amkhat); maybe one of them got agelessness out of it and likes their Brujah with some fava beans and a nice Chianti.<br /> <br /> A Wraith with a capital P Passion for culinary delights would be extremely tragic for the poor soul. Not only could they only experience it by proxy, their craving for lost ingredients and dishes would only get worse in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T15:18:32-07:00","id":1550709,"title":"","content":"Even for the Wraith, you're in trouble if your Passion is &quot;comfort foods from my youth,&quot; but less so if your Passion is, &quot;exploring culinary experiences.&quot;<br /> <br /> But even then, there are foods that humans have been eating for as long as we can prove what people actually eating. Otzi was found with jerky in his stomach. So humans have been making jerky for at least 5,000 years. It also gets really dependent on how specific you are.<br /> <br /> It's kinda like the Ventrue feeding flaw in that sense. In theory it could be so broad some Ventrue barely notice it, while others have such specific tastes they probably don't last long as vampires. But most PCs are going to be some reasonable place in the middle of the spectrum.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> While I rarely recommend reading comments sections, the third video has people from Germany and Austria pointing out that all of those so-called &quot;lost&quot; foods are common place in their equivalents of farmers markets. They might not be popular in franchise supermarkets, but there's enough people that buy them for farmers to make sure that they keep growing them on a small scale basis alongside more profitable crops.<br /> <br /> Things like the Romans eating Silphium into extinction is extremely rare. Most foods keep being grown and eaten even if they fall out of fashion in mainstream culture and finding it gets harder; it rarely gets impossible. It usually means the foods go back to being local food items instead of things grown/traded over large areas because they're popular in other cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T02:18:50-07:00","id":1550834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550664-have-you-ever-considered-the-difference-between-ancient-and-modern-foods-in-roleplay?p=1550701#post1550701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Vampires and the rare old Ghoul, the problem is that their blood thirst kind of overshadows most other passions they might have, but I think especially food if they still can consume it..</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a bit forgotten secondary skill from &quot;Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand&quot;.on page 70, named &quot;Blood Preparation&quot;:<br /> <br /> <b>BLOOD PREPARATION</b><br /> You know the effects of various substances on the blood. You can use this knowledge to recognize foreign substances in any blood you taste, and you also know the art of feeding your victims certain substances to get the desired taste and effects. You are knowledgeable in chemicals, intoxicants, herbs, spices and food and how they affect mortal and inmortal blood. You can prepare a variety of flavours for blood feasts, and are capable of combining this art with Toxicology to make the blood of a living mortal dangerous to the Kindred.<br /> * Novice: You are a dabller; you can prepare simple meals.<br /> ** Practiced: Yot know several recipes and can perpare a variety of meals.<br /> *** Competent: You know many recipes, though you have trouble preparing truly exotic cusine.<br /> **** Expert: You are and excellent chef; you know all the great recipes as well as a wide range of exotic recipes.<br /> ***** Master: You are a master chef; you know a great variety of recipes and you can create your own masterpieces.<br /> Possesed by: Some Toreador, Sabbat, Baba Yaga's chefs, Black Hand Kindred and some cannibals.<br /> Specialities: Intoxicants, Spices, Easy-to-prepare meals, Kindred Poisons, Recognizing and Analysing Tastes.<br /> <br /> Blood foods, blood-bread, blood-puding, blood-wine, several blood sweets... a nice feast is always fun in an Elysium or in an Elder's banquet hall especially if your host is on the Via Voluptarius/Path of Pleasure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Vampire parties can be fun<br /> <br /> I can easly see a Vampire with interest in the culinary arts even as a connection to his human side (and maybe even eating merit) and the various foods and herbs effects on the blood (especially if he is a Kiasyd bartender/party host with their new V20 interest in alchemy)<br /> Or one that would want to preserve the original spices or fruits, vegetables, - for example watermelons changed drastically, like eggplants, and such a vampire could have seeds of the original carefully preserving the original versions in their gardens<br /> Or jus ta cling to the past, fondly remembering the childhood when carrots were different","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-08-2025, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}